    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d466">

                <pb facs="0550" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.428/45a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spring
                            Rice</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1906</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 21, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to my note No. 1889 of
                    the 13th instant, advising you of the selection of Dr. Hugh M. Smith, the
                    Commissioner of Fisheries, and Mr. Edwin F. Sweet, the Assistant Secretary of
                    Commerce, as representatives of the United States in the proposed conference to
                    consider pending questions concerning the fisheries on both the Atlantic and
                    Pacific coasts, I have now the honor to inform you that, in deference to the
                    wish of the Canadian Government that each Government should be represented in
                    the conference by three commissioners, as stated in your personal letter to me
                    of October 30,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d466-f1"/> the Honorable William C.
                    Redfield, Secretary of Commerce, will participate in the conference as a
                    representative of the United States in addition to Doctor Smith and Mr.
                    Sweet.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
